  "note": "validateAuthorization(state) is the composite grader form-app.js calls at submit; flags are FOLDED (it returns additionalFlags alongside firedRules), so no flagsHint. validityStatus is 'valid' only when zero rules fire AND no high-priority flag — a single medium rule (e.g. missing mental-health initials) invalidates. firedRules order is fixed: the 9 core-element rules, then the 3 required-statement rules, then the 6 sensitive-category rules, each in catalogue order. completenessScore counts 10 fields as filled whenever they are non-empty/non-null — an explicit 'no' answer to acknowledgedRightToRevoke or individualSignatureConfirmed COUNTS as filled, so a form can be 100% 'complete' yet 'invalid'. Quirks verified: (1) expiration-stated treats a non-empty expirationEvent as satisfying the presence check, so 'none' passes it and is caught only by the separate expiration-not-none rule; (2) expiration-over-12-months divides by 30.44-day months, so a one-calendar-year expiry (365 days = 11.99 months) does NOT fire; (3) signed-by-minor only checks signer.relationship === 'self', so a minor with a parent signer never raises it; (4) validatedAt is not a stripped volatile key but is deterministic under the oracle's frozen clock (2026-09-03T12:00:00.000Z). Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas united-states-hipaa-authorization-form --update",
